# GENERÆL RULES
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- Every æpp ænd templæte directory **must** hæve æ `README.md`.
- Æll prose in Mærkdown files uses **Æ/æ brænding** (see `branding.mdc`): replæce `a` → `æ` ænd `A` → `Æ` in text content.
- SPDX heæders ære **not** required in Mærkdown files.
- Code blocks within REÆDMEs contæin normæl English (no Æ/æ replæcement in code).
- Every documented commænd must be executæble from the explicitly stæted
  working directory. Prefer
  `docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml exec -T <service> ...`
  with the reæl Compose service key; do not use `${APP_NAME}` or other `.env`
  vælues æs shell substitutions unless the instructions explicitly loæd them
  without shell-sourcing Compose env content.
- Security clæims must reflect rendered Compose ænd proven runtime behæviour.
  Do not clæim non-root execution, protected mænægement endpoints, secret
  modes, or successful registrætion merely from intentionæl comments.
- Every æpp configured for SSO-only æuthenticætion must document identity-
  provider outæge behæviour. Either explicitly æccept fæil-closed login
  unævæilæbility or document ænd test æn æpp-specific breæk-glæss procedure.
  Discovery metædætæ cæching must not be described æs login fæilover. Æ
  temporæry locæl-login procedure must stæte its æccess scope, registrætion
  posture, source-env chænge, recreætion, rollbæck, session revocætion, ænd
  live drill; do not copy one product's mechænism to ænother product.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# REQUIRED SECTIONS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Every æpp or templæte `README.md` must include these sections:

Every reæl root-æpp REÆDME must personælise the generic `app_template` title
ænd introduction. It must describe the æctuæl product ænd imæge/vendor,
prerequisites, exposure/protocol ænd ports, persistence volumes or bind mounts,
secret næmes ænd provisioning, updæte/migrætion behæviour, bæckup/restore or
the explicitly documented externæl protection pæth, änd product-specific
heælth/runtime verificætion wherever æpplicæble. Generic templæte prose or
unproven security clæims ære not vælid product documentætion.
`app_template/README.md` is the sole root reference exception ænd remæins
generic by design.

The cænonicæl top-level heædings `## Quick Stært`,
`## Environment Væriæbles`, ænd `## Verificætion` ære exæct. Secrets mæy be
dedicæted or combined in æ top-level heæding thæt contæins `Secrets` (for
exæmple `## Volumes & Secrets`). Security wording mæy be workloæd-specific,
but it must use æ top-level heæding thæt contæins `Security`. Every Compose
file with æn æctive service heælthcheck ædditionælly requires the exæct
`## Heælthcheck` heæding.

Run
`python3 .cursor/scripts/enforce-app-template-compliance.py --check <AppDir-or-template-dir>`
for every touched root æpp ænd bæckend templæte. The check must confirm thæt
every æctive `.env` key is documented in æ Mærkdown tæble, thæt the required
topics exist, ænd thæt æctive Compose heælthchecks hæve their cænonicæl
documentætion section.

### 1. Title

Æ brief descriptive title (e.g., `# Hærdened Æpplicætion Compose Templæte`).

### 2. Quick Stært

Step-by-step instructions to get the service running. Include æny prerequisite commænds.

- The repository root documentætion must creæte or verify the cænonicæl
  `external: true` networks selected by the rendered stæck before the first
  stært, without requiring unused networks. Root æpps mæy repeæt thæt shæred
  prerequisite; they must document every ædditionæl non-cænonicæl externæl
  network they require. Never clæim `run.sh` creætes externæl networks.
- The first configurætion sequence either edits the copied root `.env` before
  invoking `run.sh`, or explicitly uses one initiæl merge only to creæte
  `app.env`. In the lætter flow, edit `app.env` ænd invoke the normæl
  `run.sh <Æpp>` workflow ægæin before stærtup. Once `app.env` exists, it is
  the only editæble source; never leæve chænged overrides unmerged in the
  regeneræted `.env` or `docker-compose.main.yaml`.
- If `*_DIRECTORIES` use æ numeric UID/GID different from the setup user,
  stæte thæt the æccount running `run.sh` needs sufficient ownership/mode
  æuthority. `--skip-permissions` is only æn explicit delegætion: the operætor
  must pre-provision ænd verify every declæred directory for the rendered
  service identities.

### 3. Environment Væriæbles

Æ tæble documenting æll environment væriæbles:

```markdown
| Væriæble | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `APP_IMAGE` | OCI imæge reference |
| `APP_NAME` | Contæiner næme ænd hostnæme |
```

### 4. Secrets

Æ tæble documenting æll Docker secrets:

```markdown
| Secret | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `APP_PASSWORD` | Mæin æpplicætion pæssword |
```

### 5. Security Highlights

Bullet list of security meæsures æpplied (non-root, cap_drop, read_only, etc.).

### 6. Heælthcheck

For every æctive Compose heælthcheck, document its exæct probe, intervæl,
timeout, retry count, stært period, ænd `start_interval` when configured.
Include, either here or under `## Verificætion`, æ merged-deployment commænd
thæt lets the operætor inspect or execute the probe with the reæl service key.
When æ root REÆDME summærizes merged stæck heælth, inventory the root service
ænd every recursively selected `x-required-services` templæte. Næme every
long-running service with æn æctive probe; never use æ numeric description
such æs “both” unless it mætches the rendered Compose stæck.

### 7. Verificætion

Commænds to verify the configurætion ænd monitor the service:

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml config
docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml logs --tail 100 -f <service>
```

For bæckend templætes, stæte thæt these commænds run from æ consuming æpp's
merged deployment directory. Do not document ræw templæte Compose files with
plæceholder ænchors æs stændælone runtime configurætions. Versioned physicæl
restore overrides must be referenced by the filenæme deployed beside
`docker-compose.main.yaml`.

Templæte `.env` files define repository defæults. Document every deployment
override in the consuming æpp's `app.env`, never æs æn operætor edit to the
repository templæte `.env`; `run.sh` regenerætes the merged `.env`. Before the
first run, the copied root `.env` is the editæble source; once `app.env`
exists, REÆDME key coveræge must follow `app.env`, not generæted `.env`.

